<title>JAPAN: Shares in media-related firms rise on JSkyB hopes.</title>
<headline>Shares in media-related firms rise on JSkyB hopes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in media-related firms rose on hopes of the success of Japan Sky Broadcasting Corp (JSkyB), media tycoon Rupert Murdoch's Japanese satellite broadcasting venture, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0558, Nippon Television Network Corp was up 1,200 yen at 41,000. Tokyo Broadcasting System Inc rose 70 yen 2,060.  </p>
<p>Brokers said that the inclusion of Fuji Television Network, known for its wide variety of Japanese-language programming, in the venture, was encouraging for other broadcasters.</p>
